Z||000000||Songman||11-20-2000||01:26 AM||||Here's one for you guys...<P>I have a broken blinker/headlight switch on my Lexus. I bought a new assembly to put on the steering column but now I am kinda worried about the airbag. Anybody know a good (and safe) way to do this? If I disconnect the battery can I safely take apart the steering column without deploying the airbag? Thanks for any advice.||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||11-20-2000||09:17 AM||||even with the battery disconnected they air bag can STILL pop. as long as you unplug the bag from the steering wheel you'll be ok... do you have a grounding strap? (according to Chip Sewell-service manager- of Nalley Lexus here in marietta, ga.)(a wire that grounds you to the car so it won't arc if there is any static electricity) once you un plug it you'll be fine. and just grab the steering wheel puller.. yank it off and take the nice leather padded plastic off the colum. replace your part and re-assemble. just make sure you are grounded to the car!!! if you arc both your airbag, your ear drums and the side of your face will be TOAST! Yes the do get hot and they will burn your face. (like rug burn) My fater had a 94 LS, hit a guard rail and had a sunglasses imprint in his face for about 2 weeks! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||11-20-2000||06:08 PM||||I was told to just unplug the negative battery terminal and wait at least 4 min. and then I would be fine. I never had a problem so far. 90' ES||||reg||1
Z||000003||Songman||11-21-2000||01:56 PM||||Thanks guys! It's still pretty scary though. And I hate airbags anyway! I wish they would just put a switch on them that allows you to turn them on or off.... I mean, it should be my choice. It hurts no one but me.. Guess that gets back into that political arena again though... heheh||||reg||14
